WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:09.450
When I'm designing
jewelry, I feel connected.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.840
I go off into my own world,
I guess I feel at peace.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.140
I have a lot of fun
putting things together

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.930
in ways that are unexpected.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:23.010
I like scale, I like color, I
like shapes, I like textures.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.810 position:66%
There's something really interesting about

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.810
how you can put things together
in ways that are surprising.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.720 position:58%
Creating things is like my life flow,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.010
like that's what makes me happy,

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.020
it's how I feel connected back

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.183
to everything else is by creating.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.300
My name is Lauren Harwell Godfrey,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.060
and I am a fine jewelry designer.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.620
Harwell Godfrey is known

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.590
for its maximalist kind
of approach to jewelry,

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.530
very colorful, very
intricate with patterns,

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.500
a lot of details, and
I would say geometric

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.450
is also a word that comes to mind.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.400
I like fitting things together

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.193 position:59%
in this geometric kind of pattern way.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:07.830
I talk a lot about my work

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.500 position:61%
being inspired by the African diaspora.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.570
I'm certainly inspired by travel.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:15.030 position:64%
Trips to Morocco and India and, you know,

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:18.300
places where the handicrafts
are just so robust

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.003
have certainly influenced
the work that I like to do.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.390
We are in my studio right now,

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:25.980
which is in Northern California,

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:29.040
but I do a lot of my
production in New York,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.480 position:56%
that's kind of the predominant place

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.303
where production happens in
actually making the jewelry.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.310
Well, the piece that
I'm taking you through

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.860
are my 5 Stone Totem Drop Huggies,

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.180
which is a pair of earrings

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.670 position:58%
and they're very gemmy, they're long,

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.340
there's different colors
used in interesting ways,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.970
there's different types of
stones, there's different shapes.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:53.010 position:58%
It's maximalist, it kind of goes back

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.080 position:56%
to all the things that I love to do.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.230
I started with a sketch and I
actually sketched those out.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.660 position:58%
I find that my greatest success comes

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.204 position:66%
when I'm as specific as possible with them

00:02:03.204 --> 00:02:05.070 position:59%
to getting that end piece to look like

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.170
what I had in my head.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.460
And then, from that point,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.110 position:61%
we take that and we have a CAD designer

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:12.480
that we really like to
work with who gets our work

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.980
and knows how we like things.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.560
So we get these files where
you can turn things around

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.010
and look at them in 3D, so it
gives me a really good sense.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.760
Then we make either a silver
casting or a wax casting,

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.370
and for these, we did
silver, so it's very easy

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.280
to like take those around and
like set stones into them.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.310
And I also drew an inspiration
for colors that I wanted

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:33.990
and I was like, these
are generally speaking

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.520
the colors that I want.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.230 position:66%
But then I had to go and find those stones

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.520
to fit those colors,

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.070
and there was like a price
point that I'm trying to hit

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.240 position:58%
so there's all these different things

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.500
that inform the stones.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.940
So we had to go out,

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.073 position:63%
find the right sources for those stones.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:49.950
Hi.
Hey, welcome.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:51.842
Good to see you.
You too.

00:02:51.842 --> 00:02:54.270
I have different gem dealers
that I like to work with

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.640
and I feel like those relationships
have really, you know,

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.384
developed over time, and me,
like, learning more about

00:02:59.384 --> 00:03:01.680
their process and where
things are coming from

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.550
and how they're sourcing

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.500 position:59%
and just kind of seeing their overall,

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.600
you know, what they have to offer.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.440
Thinking that like maybe we
do like a big stone up here.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.360
Here's a different green
that's a little smaller.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.830
Yeah, it's quite a specimen,

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.683
so that would be really incredible.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.220
Sometimes people actually
like reach out to me

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.990
and just introduce themselves

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.180
so they kind of come in
from different places,

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.250 position:64%
but then over time, as you work with them

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.560
and you see their goods and
you learn more about, you know,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.660
what they're up to,
you figure out the ones

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.690 position:63%
that like most closely align to my needs

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.880
from like the colors
and the kinds of stones

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:38.430
and the scale of the stones
that I like to work with to,

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:39.840
you know, does this fit in

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.910
with kind of the overall
vision that I have

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.320 position:58%
for the brand and the types of people

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.893
that I wanna work with
and, you know, support?

00:03:45.893 --> 00:03:48.933 position:56%
I think I am going to go with these.

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.110
Okay.
Thank you.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:53.910
There are a lot of things
that have contributed

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:55.533
to the person that I am now.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.760
I was born and raised
in Southern California,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.480
and my parents divorced when
I was young, when I was four,

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.330
so I was really raised
predominantly by my mom,

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.100 position:61%
and my grandmother was very much around

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.533
so a lot of very strong
women in the house.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.250
My grandmother would
wear jewelry every day

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.870 position:58%
and in fact I have a ring that I made

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.790 position:56%
that I'm wearing today that she wore

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.280
in a different form every
day as a cocktail ring.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.240
I made it into a band

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.520 position:61%
that I could stack with my wedding ring

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:25.773
and just kind of always
think of her with it.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.160
I knew I wanted to do
something in the arts,

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.930
I knew I wanted to get paid for it,

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:33.900
and advertising felt like
this really great fit for me.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.103 position:61%
I worked in that industry for 15 years,

00:04:36.103 --> 00:04:37.500
I worked really hard

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.730
and I just realized that I
had been burning myself out

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:45.210 position:64%
for a long time and I kind of hit a wall.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:48.060
I knew that there were other
things inside of me creatively

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.577
that I wanted to explore. That
led me to culinary school.

00:04:51.577 --> 00:04:56.577
So this winding road of
my careers and passions.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:01.560
But I wasn't figuring out what
I could add to that picture

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:05.280
that was gonna be compelling
and interesting and different.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.540
So I took a step back and
made myself a necklace

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.400 position:66%
and I made it out of leather and crystals,

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.650
it was very like festival wear

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:16.230
and I wore it to a festival

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.210
but people saw it and they
thought it was interesting

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.390
and I started getting
requests for those necklaces.

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:23.760
There's just something in
how it made me feel inside

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.460
and how I felt working
with those materials

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.220
and thinking in that way, like
these little mini sculptures.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.070
And that's not a way I had
ever really thought before

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:35.043
and I really just felt
myself so compelled by it.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:41.070
Typically, when I have the
castings and I have the stones,

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.690 position:56%
it goes into production essentially,

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.020
and that means that it's getting
made and being assembled.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.810
We gather the stones and then
we move them to our setter.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:51.390
There's nothing like
working with somebody who's,

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:53.610
you know, a master at
working with their hands.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:55.110
It's precious metals,

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.390 position:66%
it's precious materials, it's soft stones,

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.450
we need technical masters
to be able to do this work

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.270 position:59%
and that's what makes it fine jewelry.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:06.570 position:64%
So once that we get that seated in there,

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:09.483
we can hammer the wall
over, make the stone tight.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:13.620 position:58%
Our setter will receive those stones,

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:16.050 position:64%
those loose stones and our rough castings

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.450 position:59%
and he will actually go to the process

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.160
of buffing 'em up a little bit,

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:23.040
pre-polishing so that
they're easier to work with.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.290
And those castings are actually
really rough at this point,

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:27.780
they're gold, but they're
not at all polished

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.790 position:63%
and he'll actually do some pre-polishing

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:31.020 position:56%
so that they're easier to work with.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.330
And he uses sandpaper,
he has a rubber wheel,

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.013
just things to clean it up a bit.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.770
Once that's all done,

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.860
he'll start to get ready to
set that stone into that piece.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.750
So he uses a shellac stick,

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.670 position:63%
and he makes it to the exact right shape

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.380
of the thing we are working on.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:49.233
Get it nice and gooey so it sticks,

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.883
and we'll put it in place.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:59.403
Now it's prepared for
us to put the stone in.

00:06:59.403 --> 00:07:01.680
Then after that casting is secured,

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.540 position:61%
he'll actually start setting the stone,

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:06.150
and what he wants to do is take
a little bit of that bezel,

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:09.150
and like get a little
lip of it over each stone

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:10.743
so he uses a micro hammer.

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:12.990
Once the stone is secured,

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.490 position:61%
there's some cleanup that has to happen

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:16.350
because of all that hammering

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:19.710
so he actually uses a tool that,
it's like an engraving tool

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.480
that cleans the wall of the bezel,

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.280 position:61%
and he actually has a way of buffing it

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.770
so he can buff out all of
those like hammer marks.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:26.970
They're small but they're there

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:29.340
so gotta clean those marks up.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.530 position:61%
Once all these pieces are put together,

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.120
we then connect those jump rings

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.270
to make the earring like a
whole piece and complete.

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:39.000
And then, finally, we
actually do a final polish

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.093
to make the gold really
beautiful and and sparkly.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:49.920
Hi.
How you doing?

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:50.956
Good to see you.

00:07:50.956 --> 00:07:53.370
After production is over
and the earrings are done,

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:55.500 position:61%
they come back to me and I inspect them

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.180
and just get to see the final thing

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:59.700 position:64%
and make sure it's what I had in my mind.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.643
Oh, that's so pretty,
very clean, very nice.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.850 position:56%
I love how the colors came together,

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:08.880
I like that interplay of
opaque versus transparent.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:10.950
We call these a totem earring

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:13.320
because I think there's
something totem-esque about them,

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:14.700
the way that they are these things

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.230 position:63%
that are stacked up on top of each other

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.894
in these different and
interesting shapes and colors.

00:08:17.894 --> 00:08:19.495
Thank you, Set.
You're welcome,

00:08:19.495 --> 00:08:21.510
it was my pleasure.

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:24.060 position:61%
I think designing jewelry has taught me

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.873
to really trust myself.

00:08:25.873 --> 00:08:28.590 align:start position:0% line:0%
It's really, it's been
an interesting process

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:30.720 position:59%
because you truly are making something

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.406 position:56%
for people to buy, a specific thing,

00:08:33.406 --> 00:08:35.970 position:59%
and when people get excited about that

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:39.270
and connect to it, it's validating

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:40.110
in the sense that you're like,

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:42.420
oh wow, you know, I'm not crazy,

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:43.710
this thing that I think is cool

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.701
is cool and interesting
to someone else too.

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:50.700
I have always been
interested in philanthropy.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:52.470
There's just something
about making something

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:54.750
that's so, you know,
it's such a luxury good,

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:56.610 position:64%
it's expensive, there's all these things,

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.440
and yet the reality in our world

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:01.350
is that there are people
suffering and and hurting.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:05.310
And so, I felt like I had
this unique opportunity

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:08.610
to take those luxury goods
that people were coveting

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:11.070
and actually turn that into money

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.530
that I could donate back
to these organizations.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:16.470
So I actually donate a
hundred percent of the profits

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:19.500
from the Charity Hearts, is
the collection that I call it.

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.870
And I don't know, there's
this interesting collection

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:26.070
of people who seem to be getting
behind it, which is cool.

00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:30.870
Kamala Harris wearing my
NAACP heart was super cool.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:34.470
I chose the NAACP as the charity
that I wanted to donate to

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:36.120
'cause I believe in the
work that they're doing,

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.100
especially from a legal standpoint

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:39.780 position:56%
and how important that is to create,

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:40.620
you know, an environment

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:43.560
where black justice
actually comes to fruition.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.500
Hilary Swank, Blake
Lively actually did a lot

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:49.322
to promote the heart for
Everytown for Gun Safety,

00:09:49.322 --> 00:09:51.810
so did Julianne Moore.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:53.220
The last one I just introduced

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:56.010
is for Everytown for Gun Safety.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:00.360
And as a mother and a human
and just a person who,

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.510
you know, values safety and
wants everyone to be safe,

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:06.753
I think we need to have
common sense gun laws.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:11.670
I think that giving back
is just something that,

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.920
again, that I've believed
in for a really long time

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.860
and this feels to me like
the right way to do it.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:19.590
I know that the stuff that I make

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.432 position:66%
is not something that everyone can afford,

00:10:21.432 --> 00:10:23.070
and then I actually try to price

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:26.910
these particular pieces
to be very approachable

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:30.120 position:64%
for within the fine jewelry luxury world,

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:31.530
so that I can sell, you know,

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:34.770
as many of them as I can and
be able to donate that money.

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:38.880
I feel like creating and
designing really brings me

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.250
into the thing I feel like
I'm supposed to be doing,

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:44.040
and there's something about
that that's really satisfying

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:47.040
and I just feel like I'm
a part of something bigger

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:48.290
when I'm doing that work.

